WEBVTT

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:13.800
Hey.

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:18.180
-You brought your buddies today?
-Pardon?

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:22.390
What!

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.020
Who are those people?

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.060
What do you want?

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.020
Soliciting? No thanks.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.360
I'll take this. Don't interfere.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:34.530
All right.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.030
I see it... a fighter’s spirit.

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.910
Wait, hold on a second.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:44.160
Is it possible that he is Ivan Karaev?

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.420
You know him?

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:50.340
He's a Russian kickboxer
who's been standing out recently.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.300
What is he doing here?

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.010
Nothing personal.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.090
This is just business.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.850
You're going to have to stay in bed
for a while.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.680
Watch out, Ohma!

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.980
Ivan's high-kick is known as
the Reaper's Sickle.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.240
You did too many high-kicks
and forgot about defense.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.990
You are a diligent fighter.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.240
So?

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:23.500
You want to fight, too?

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:26.210
You're really good.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:28.460
I like it.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:30.670
Huh?

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.800
I told you not to interfere.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:35.800
You can't beat him down.

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:39.800
Don't you dare look down on--

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.730
<i>With that amount of blood loss,</i>
<i>he must have got the arteries.</i>

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.820
Jeez. He's useless.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:56.610
I hate to watch a loser struggle in vain.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.860
Be careful, Ohma.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:01.740
He's got a knife with him.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:05.540
Relax, pops. We didn't come here to fight.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.540
I'm Lihito.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:11.670
I'm going to be your opponent
in the upcoming <i>kengan </i>match.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.210
Oh.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.670
By the way, my real name is undisclosed.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:19.470
<i>L... Lihito?</i>

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:22.800
<i>He's going to be Ohma's opponent?</i>

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:27.520
<i>He seems like an interesting dude.</i>
<i>I'm excited to fight with him.</i>

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:02.950
SUPER HUMAN

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:11.960
THE DAY OF THE <i>KENGAN </i>MATCH

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:26.140
KAZUO YAMASHITA
NOGI PUBLICATIONS

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:29.640
Good to see you again, Mr. Nogi.

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.060
Is that Komada's replacement?

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:34.980
I can see a good fighter's spirit in him.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.560
Mr. Yoshitake, I'm sorry to tell you,

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:40.820
but we are going to win again today.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:45.610
I like your confidence.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:49.120
But don't underestimate Lihito.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.160
That's Yoshiro Yoshitake.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:55.710
He's the white hope
of the real estate industry.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:58.750
Excuse me, Ms. Akiyama?

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:02.170
What is the wager on today's match?

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.170
You haven't heard?

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:05.590
Well, no...

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:09.760
They're wagering the construction rights
to the New Makunouchi Building,

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:13.100
a skyscraper to be built here
after the demolition of this building.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:16.940
The total project cost is going to be
around 100 billion yen.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:20.980
A hundred billion yen?

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:24.740
<i>Their sense of money is</i>
<i>in a whole other universe.</i>

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:30.200
<i>What's about to happen</i>
<i>is not just a fistfight.</i>

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:33.200
<i>It's a 100-billion-yen slugfest!</i>

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:55.520
Sir, who are those people?

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:59.060
They are members of
the <i>Kengan </i>Association.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:00.270
What is that?

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:04.320
It's the operating committee
of <i>kengan </i>matches.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:07.780
All the members are the heads of
prestigious companies.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:12.580
<i>Right. They sure look like billionaires.</i>

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:18.290
It's customary for the association members
to come out and witness the match results.

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.960
But that's just an ostensible reason.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:24.920
These matches have always been
a source of entertainment, too.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:29.930
Frankly speaking,
they bet on the match results.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:34.890
You can see they get more heated
when money is involved.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.890
Who the hell is that guy
fighting for the Nogi Group?

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:40.900
-What happened to Komada?
-We want him!

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:44.480
-Lihito!
-Show us another brutal fight.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:49.150
Lihito's on five wins and no losses.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.320
He's quite a popular fighter now.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.870
Do you think it was really a good idea?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.200
What was?

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:59.290
We didn't tell Ohma
about Lihito's secret weapon.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.420
It doesn't matter.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:04.170
This match is a litmus test
for Ohma Tokita.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.210
If he can't be the winner,

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:11.890
he will never be the standard-bearer
to lead me to my ambitious goals.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:14.720
Are you ready?

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:20.310
Yo, Tokita. I feel bad for you guys.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:23.230
Your boss is going to lose
a lot of money for sure.

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:26.150
You're looking good today.

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.940
I'm glad that I waited until today
to beat you up.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:35.330
Ready, set...

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:46.920
Fight!

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:54.140
-Just start fighting now!
-Why aren't you moving?

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:55.850
Do your freaking job!

00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:58.520
They are not moving.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:01.690
You're wrong.
They've already started fighting.

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:05.190
Watching.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:06.860
Shifting weight.

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:08.110
Taking stances.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:12.860
They've been tuning up
since before the match started.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:19.040
Constraining each other's movement
resulted in a deadlock.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.710
<i>It's almost like a face-off</i>
<i>between two master fencers</i>

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:25.460
<i>where a single stroke of sword</i>
<i>determines the winner.</i>

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:30.090
They're watching for the right moment
to initiate an attack.

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:32.550
<i>Ohma.</i>

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:40.220
<i>Mr. Nogi, you are going to be</i>
<i>a stepping stone</i>

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:43.350
<i>to my further growth.</i>

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:57.660
<i>They'll move.</i>

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:01.870
-Both moved!
-Ohma was faster.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.210
He endured Ohma's punch.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:11.960
He moved toward the blow

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:16.550
to throw Ohma's timing off
and reduced the damage.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:21.560
In addition, he has his own
unique and eccentric blows.

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:24.270
He has innate abilities
of both offense and defense.

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:28.810
Lihito's on an incredibly
high level as a striker.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:32.150
However...

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:38.910
Yes!

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:46.160
If this was just a fistfight, nobody
would stand a chance of beating Lihito.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:48.210
But this is more than that.

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:49.540
No way. Lihito's losing.

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:51.710
That Ohma guy's strong.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.920
<i>You're a pretty good fighter.</i>

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:58.130
<i>But I've taken down so many fighters</i>
<i>who were as good as you.</i>

00:09:58.260 --> 00:09:59.760
You're nailing it, Ohma!

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:01.810
He's barely hanging on.

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.020
Is this all you got?

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:18.660
What happened?

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:21.620
He's bleeding as if
a blade gouged out his flesh.

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:22.950
<i>He used it.</i>

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:25.580
<i>Let's see if it gives Lihito an advantage</i>

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.250
<i>or not.</i>

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:30.580
<i>This shape of the scar...</i>

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.170
You scraped off my flesh

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:34.590
with your fingertips.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:41.930
<i>There are three major kinds of</i>
<i>grip strengths.</i>

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:46.430
<i>Firstly, crushing power is the strength</i>
<i>to squeeze objects by hand.</i>

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.520
<i>Secondly, holding power is the strength</i>
<i>to catch hold of objects.</i>

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:55.400
<i>Lastly, pinching power is</i>
<i>the strength of fingertips.</i>

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:59.530
<i>Lihito's pinching power is</i>
<i>far beyond human capabilities.</i>

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:04.450
<i>Climbing up a sheer cliff is</i>
<i>as easy as falling off a log for him.</i>

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:06.950
<i>He truly is a superhuman!</i>

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:11.120
<i>Imagine what would happen if he used</i>
<i>the superhuman power to attack people.</i>

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:15.090
<i>Wherever Lihito's finger touches</i>
<i>becomes their vital spot.</i>

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:20.970
<i>Whether it's flesh or bone,</i>
<i>he can cut through it.</i>

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:23.720
<i>His fingers cut as sharply as razors.</i>

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:27.560
<i>That's his special ability,</i>
<i>which is called:</i>

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:30.480
<i>the Razor's Edge.</i>

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:32.980
Play time is over!

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:36.770
Lihito, rip him up with your Razor's Edge!

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:42.280
<i>The crowds know about his ability.</i>
<i>This isn't his first time doing that.</i>

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:45.030
<i>That man kept this from me</i>
<i>on purpose, huh?</i>

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.790
You better focus on me.

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:51.620
In return for beating me up
so many times earlier,

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:53.580
I'm going to mince you into pieces.

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:55.040
<i>I see.</i>

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:59.880
<i>That wasn't a knife</i>
<i>but Lihito's technique.</i>

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:05.850
<i>I have no idea how it works but he can</i>
<i>rip human flesh apart with his hand.</i>

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:08.510
<i>What is Ohma going to do?</i>

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:12.890
<i>Is there a way to get</i>
<i>the upper hand on the razor?</i>

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:21.280
Take him down, Lihito!

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:30.620
<i>He's bleeding too much.</i>

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:32.750
<i>He can't last much longer.</i>

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:39.090
Don't let yourself get carried away!

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:46.050
-What's wrong?
-Just beat him!

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:48.600
That's one hell of a kick.

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:52.850
Good thing I put my right hand in
when you kicked me.

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:56.600
Now you're the loser.

00:12:57.310 --> 00:13:00.400
<i>He attacked Ohma while getting kicked?</i>

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:04.990
<i>What a guy! He's like an armed beast.</i>

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:07.620
<i>He's completely guarded.</i>

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:11.580
Lihito has no blind spots.

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:14.870
He can hit, dodge and shave flesh off.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:18.130
Prepare to be diced.

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:22.510
You managed to protect
your tendon from me?

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:25.220
Good job, human.

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:27.390
Did you call me human?

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:30.390
-It sounds like you are not--
-That's right.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:35.310
I'm not a human.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:40.820
I was 11 years old
when I first tore a coin apart.

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:44.070
I didn't train myself for that.

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:46.110
I could just do it.

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:52.740
So, that means I was born
with my pinching power.

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:54.950
Do you understand?

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:57.540
I'm on a whole different level of strength

00:13:57.620 --> 00:14:00.840
from you and the others
from the beginning.

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:06.840
For a human, you did well
fighting against a superhuman like me.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:11.720
I'll tell you my real name as your reward.

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:15.520
It's Ichiro Nakata.

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:19.730
That's a good name.
Why did you change it to Lihito?

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:24.150
Superheroes don't use
their real names, you know?

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:29.070
As a superhuman,
I decided to go by a hero name.

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:32.870
Lihito means a man
who surpasses human principles.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:35.240
Just like me, huh?

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:36.660
LIHITO

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:39.290
You're such a chatterbox.

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:42.880
A hero doesn't speak much.

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:44.050
What?

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:47.920
You're the superhuman?
Don't talk nonsense.

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:51.640
Humans aren't that easy
for the likes of you to surpass.

00:14:53.510 --> 00:14:58.940
Says the man who's powerless
before my Razor's Edge.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:01.350
I've found a way to beat it.

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:06.780
I was waiting to see
if you have other abilities.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:08.280
You disappointed me.

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:18.450
Hey, you're in my space.

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:29.550
Lihito, finish him off!

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:31.550
You don't need to tell me.

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:34.510
I'll mince you.

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:37.560
-We've won!
-Good.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:45.110
It didn't work?

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:46.860
What the hell?

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:55.160
<i>Lihito's pinch grip surely is incredible.</i>

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:58.910
<i>But in order to rip through things,</i>

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:02.500
<i>it requires distance for acceleration</i>
<i>in addition to finger strength.</i>

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:06.250
<i>In other words,</i>
<i>without having enough distance,</i>

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:09.300
<i>he can't even cut through tofu.</i>

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:15.180
Now you're just a human,
Ichiro Nakata.

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:23.480
He doesn't need the Razor's Edge.
He's still way stronger than Ohma.

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:25.810
It's a piece of cake.

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:43.210
<i>The association members have observed</i>
<i>many deadly </i>kengan<i> matches before.</i>

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:48.090
<i>Now they are left bewildered</i>
<i>by the inexplicable sight before them.</i>

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:55.380
<i>Lihito initiated the attacks, but somehow,</i>
<i>he's being attacked.</i>

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:03.310
<i>Apart from Lihito, few spectators</i>
<i>noticed what's happening.</i>

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:12.400
<i>Ohma waited for his opponent</i>
<i>to make a move</i>

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:17.620
<i>and added a few grams of pressure</i>
<i>to set Lihito's power to go off.</i>

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:22.200
<i>That disrupted the power flow,</i>
<i>making it uncontrollable.</i>

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:27.040
<i>Ohma Tokita.</i>

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:31.250
<i>This guy has perfect control</i>
<i>over the flow of power.</i>

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.510
<i>That's no human work.</i>

00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:34.760
Lihito!

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:37.010
What the hell are you doing?
Fight back!

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:39.640
That's not going to happen.

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:43.930
It's already over.

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:52.190
The match is over.

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:55.280
The winner is Ohma Tokita.

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:58.110
He won!

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:01.870
He passed... for now.

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:05.290
Lihito, did you feel it?

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:09.170
That was the technique beyond principle.

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:17.840
WINNER: OHMA OF NOGI GROUP
LOSER: LIHITO OF YOSHITAKE REAL ESTATE

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:23.260
NOGI GROUP WON THE CONSTRUCTION RIGHTS
TO THE NEW MAKUNOUCHI BUILDING

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:32.360
Here. Have another cup.

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:33.900
Thank you.

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:40.200
No, I should thank you
for bringing the money all the way here.

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:43.490
Ohma, why don't you ask them
to send it by wire transfer?

00:18:43.660 --> 00:18:45.790
I can't be bothered.

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:49.540
You are the one who's bothering her.

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:50.830
I'm fine.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:55.920
There's actually something
I wanted to ask Ohma.

00:18:57.840 --> 00:19:01.930
There are 1,205 fighters
registered to <i>kengan </i>matches.

00:19:02.260 --> 00:19:06.140
Each fighter has
8.5 matches a year on average.

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:11.020
It's five times as many as the world's
biggest combat sport organization.

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:12.770
Wow, that's a lot.

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:18.190
Besides, all the fighters are elites
the association members acknowledged.

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:21.530
Some lose their lives in brutal matches.

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:26.370
A decent amount of remuneration
is promised in return.

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:30.870
To be honest, however, it's far from
enough, considering how grueling they are.

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:35.880
Those who come into this world
of their own accord must be daredevils

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:39.050
or men with some determined purpose.

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:45.510
Ohma Tokita, what makes you compete
in <i>kengan </i>matches?

00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:51.810
My purpose?

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:55.400
Do I need a reason to fight?

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:58.610
I just want to show who's the strongest.

00:19:58.820 --> 00:19:59.940
That's all.

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:03.070
Any other reasons
are just tacked on afterwards.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:04.450
It's full of lies.

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:06.700
Is that it?

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:10.870
You know you're risking your life, right?

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:12.420
You're wrong.

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:17.750
I will only lose when hell freezes over.

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:24.720
<i>There are 1,205 kengan fighters.</i>

00:20:25.510 --> 00:20:28.060
<i>He has to be one of them.</i>

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:31.350
<i>I can't wait to see him again.</i>

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:36.480
KOUOU WOMEN'S UNIVERSITY

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:39.230
AUDITORIUM

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:43.240
TOSHIO OZU
KENGAN FIGHTER EXAMINER FOR KOUOU GROUP

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.830
This is the battle royal of
the fighter applicants

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.880
for us, Kouou Education Group.

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:01.710
How did you know about this?

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:05.300
I'll just say "people will talk."

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:09.390
You broke in and knocked out our examiner.

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:12.640
For what? To promote yourself
for the <i>kengan </i>matches?

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:14.100
I want to see him.

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:16.440
Who do you want to see?

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:21.650
I heard my old friend had
a <i>kengan </i>match recently.

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:25.860
It seems like he has some misconceptions.

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:31.910
We have a lot of catching up to do.
So I want to see him.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:37.080
Okay. You're our affiliated fighter
from now on.

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:40.920
Are you sure you can decide
such a thing so easily?

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:45.260
I'm Shion Soryuin,
the chairwoman of Kouou.

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:47.510
I'm Setsuna Kiryu.

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:50.260
Pleasure to meet you.

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:51.930
MYSTERIOUS <i>KENGAN</i> FIGHTER

00:23:23.520 --> 00:23:26.650
HEADQUARTERS OF NOGI GROUP

00:23:27.030 --> 00:23:32.620
Your company is wagering
50 billion yen on this match.

00:23:33.320 --> 00:23:40.000
Even if you did win,
all you get is a one-way ticket to hell.

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:42.290
I think it's insane.

00:23:42.710 --> 00:23:44.920
Are you really sure about this, Mr. Nogi?

00:23:45.250 --> 00:23:50.630
<i>Our opponent is the big gun who has</i>
<i>a kengan record of 57 wins and no losses.</i>

00:23:50.720 --> 00:23:51.880
Of course.

00:23:52.340 --> 00:23:54.850
We are going to win...

00:23:55.760 --> 00:23:58.640
the one-way ticket to hell.

00:23:59.810 --> 00:24:03.690
<i>Ohma, this is the final test for you.</i>

00:24:06.610 --> 00:24:08.860
<i>Wrestling fans, be proud.</i>

00:24:09.110 --> 00:24:10.530
<i>Bring back your dreams.</i>

00:24:11.110 --> 00:24:15.410
<i>The man with a perfect 57-0 record</i>
<i>meets all of those wishes.</i>

00:24:15.620 --> 00:24:18.910
<i>This is what professional wrestling is.</i>
<i>Next episode: "Tough Guy"</i>

00:24:19.430 --> 00:24:20.910
Subtitle translation by Miki Miyaji
